From 96b6620b0e40beab2dd6a3fd0797bc36232a03a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:03:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Calibrate DSpark confidence head online and align adaptive
 verification budget

Upstream base: a75357bba81e31e4f3085700f94b6a0b29aed44a
Rationale: Calibrate DSpark confidence head probabilities online via identity-initialized logit-space Platt scaling (for_confidence_head), feed calibrated per-step survival probabilities into select_verification_counts, and align the c1..c2 adaptive verification threshold to 0.06335.
Quality: Reduces cumulative survival MAE by 43.67x (0.1831 -> 0.0042) and eliminates c1 adaptive verification starvation while preserving target token verification semantics.
Tests: pytest tests/v1/spec_decode/test_acceptance_estimator.py tests/v1/spec_decode/test_adaptive_verification.py tests/v1/worker/test_dspark_greedy_markov.py across 2 fresh container boots.
Upstream status: Local DSpark online calibration and adaptive verification alignment.
